r":[0.1704,0.5637,0.037,0.0296]},{"n":"Yaoyao","r":[0.2148,0.5637,0.037,0.0296]},{"n":"Thoma","r":[0.0815,0.6178,0.037,0.0296]},{"n":"Xingqiu","r":[0.1704,0.6178,0.037,0.0296]},{"n":"Barbara","r":[0.2148,0.6178,0.037,0.0296]},{"n":"Thoma","r":[0.0815,0.6719,0.037,0.0296]},{"n":"Yoimiya","r":[0.1259,0.6719,0.037,0.0296]},{"n":"Xingqiu","r":[0.1704,0.6719,0.037,0.0296]},{"n":"Kaedehara Kazuha","r":[0.2148,0.6719,0.037,0.0296]}]}]}},"thumb":"content/genshin/builds/thoma/261111-225304/en-1.t.webp","why":{"w":[{"name":"Favonius Lance","text":"Craftable EM polearm that restores Energy after Skill, easing Burst uptime while scaling Burgeon damage. Use Burst before Skill to avoid Kitain draining Energy needed for Burst. R3–R5 preferred."},{"name":"Kitain Cross Spear","text":"Offers substantial EM for stronger Burgeon explosions, but its damage passive does not boost Burgeon itself. Only if you can meet the higher ER requirement without Kitain."},{"name":"Dragon's Bane","text":"Provides ER and team particles."},{"name":"Engulfing Lightning","text":"HP% strengthens the shield and its passive can restore Energy, letting Thoma invest elsewhere. Only useful when he receives healing during rotations."},{"name":"Rightful Reward","text":"Craftable EM alternative; its leaf can give the on-field ally ATK but does not increase Burgeon reaction damage. Best after solving Burst energy needs."},{"name":"Moonpiercer","text":"Easy HP% option for stronger shielding, not Burgeon damage or Energy restoration. Shield-support variation only; high ER needed from artifacts."}],"a":[{"names":["Flower of Paradise Lost"],"text":"Best Burgeon DMG set by a small margin.","stats":"ER or EM / EM / EM"},{"names":["Gilded Dreams"],"text":"Nearly as strong as Flower and usually more efficient to farm; grants valuable EM in mixed-element teams.","stats":"ER or EM / EM / EM"},{"names":["Gilded Dreams","Wanderer's Troupe"],"text":"Simple 160-EM bridge build while farming a complete four-piece set.","stats":"ER or EM / EM / EM"}],"t":[{"name":"Burgeon House Rules","members":["Thoma","Nahida","Xingqiu","Sangonomiya Kokomi"],"text":"Nahida and Xingqiu create Cores; Kokomi drives Hydro and heals while Thoma’s Burst triggers Burgeon.","roles":["Burgeon Trigger / Shielder","Dendro Enabler / Buffer","Off-field DPS / Hydro Enabler","Healer / Hydro Enabler"]},{"name":"Garden of Fireworks","members":["Thoma","Kamisato Ayato","Nahida","Yaoyao"],"text":"Ayato drives Hydro during Thoma’s Burst, Nahida supplies Dendro.","roles":["Shielder / Pyro Enabler","On-field DPS","Dendro Enabler / Buffer","Healer / Dendro Enabler"]},{"name":"Budget Bloom Patrol","members":["Thoma","Traveler (Dendro)","Xingqiu","Barbara"],"text":"Accessible Burgeon core: infuse Dendro Traveler’s Burst with Hydro, not Pyro.","roles":["Burgeon Trigger / Shielder","Dendro Enabler / Battery","Off-field DPS / Hydro Enabler","Healer"]},{"name":"Shielded Summer","members":["Thoma","Yoimiya","Xingqiu","Kaedehara Kazuha"],"text":"Shield-support variation: Yoimiya’s Normal Attacks refresh Thoma’s shield.","roles":["Shielder / Pyro Enabler","On-field DPS","Off-field DPS / Hydro Enabler","Buffer / Debuffer"]}],"v":"Shield Support: Favonius Lance + 4pc Noblesse; ER/HP%/HP% or CR. Keep Burst available to refresh his shield with Normal Attacks.\nHybrid Burgeon: Keep Flower or Gilded; replace an EM main stat with HP% only if additional shielding is essential. Burgeon DMG falls.\nF2P Burgeon: Kitain Cross Spear and 4pc Gilded (or 2pc EM + 2pc EM). Prioritize ER before stacking EM.\nC4 Energy Relief: C4 restores 15 Energy after Burst; adjust ER to your team and invest extra rolls in EM or HP.\nC6 Shield Buffer: C6 buffs teammates’ Normal.","n":2},"seo":{"roles":["Reaction DPS / Shield"],"about":"Thoma triggers Burgeon with coordinated Pyro strikes from his Burst, turning Dendro Cores into powerful AoE explosions. Prioritize Level 90, enough Energy Recharge to Burst consistently, then Elemental Mastery. He also offers a separate H